<title>FRANCE: French civil service pay talk timing bad - minister.</title>
<headline>French civil service pay talk timing bad - minister.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Efforts to start talks on civil service pay for 1997 and 1998 have come at a bad time because of staff representative elections in the education, hospital and prison sectors, civil service minister Dominque Perben said.</p>
<p>Perben's stance was reported in the minutes of an address to the parliamentary finance commission.</p>
<p>Civil service pay rises were frozen in 1996 and Prime Minister Alain Juppe has said he is open to talks.</p>
<p>The minutes said Perben had said there was a &quot;will on both sides to reach an agreement&quot;.</p>
</text>
